Kubeconfig for cluster test-clusters/my-cluster:

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Config
clusters:
- cluster:
    server: https://my-cluster-api.example.com:6443
  name: my-cluster
contexts:
- context:
    cluster: my-cluster
    user: my-cluster-admin
  name: my-cluster
current-context: my-cluster
users:
- name: my-cluster-admin
  user:
    client-certificate-data: dGVzdC1jZXJ0
    client-key-data: dGVzdC1rZXk=
```

To use this kubeconfig:
1. Save the content between the ``` markers to a file (e.g., cluster-kubeconfig.yaml)
2. Use it with kubectl: kubectl --kubeconfig=cluster-kubeconfig.yaml get nodes
